{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":109444,"duration_api_ms":182790,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e4ea628f-d649-4aeb-95b2-72868106d1b2","total_cost_usd":0.5507104,"usage":{"input_tokens":806,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28207,"cache_read_input_tokens":117542,"output_tokens":2936,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28207,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":189,"outputTokens":9738,"cacheReadInputTokens":950454,"cacheCreationInputTokens":75433,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.23821565000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":806,"outputTokens":2936,"cacheReadInputTokens":117542,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28207,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.31249475000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"After examining the relevant source files, I agree with the planner on all six amendments. The failing test, missing DIC validation, undocumented valid_range unit contract, dead check_ranges() production path, and incomplete per-parameter metadata coverage are all real, confirmed defects. The opt-in renormalization proposal (fr-3-70c8111f) would introduce unnecessary schema complexity and risk showing scientifically incorrect values for legacy kinetic fields whose normalization is semantically correct.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-67e7ae00","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: Engine::from_parts() calls refresh_habitat_registry() which computes light_exposure using the invalid intensity_index=1.4 before step_hours() invokes enforce_invariants(). The test's clone is taken before from_parts(), so the habitat_registry diverges. The fix should update the test expectation to account for the canonical pre-step state produced by from_parts(), not weaken the refresh behavior."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-bfd109f4","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour and photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour are defined in the struct (line 342-343) and included in param_value() (lines 533-538), but are absent from the validate() non-negative/finite array (lines 971-1116). A TOML file with NaN or negative DIC rates would silently pass validation, which could corrupt downstream chemistry calculations."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-25137feb","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: provenance_value() normalizes the stored value via normalize_process_param_for_provenance() (dividing by reference volume for legacy _mg fields), but check_ranges() compares this normalized value against the raw valid_range bounds from ParamMeta. Without documentation stating that valid_range must be in normalized units, TOML authors will naturally write bounds in serialized units and get incorrect warnings or missed violations."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-cb38a067","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: load_process_params() (lib.rs:65-75) calls only validate(), never check_ranges(). The only call sites for check_ranges() are in unit tests (presets.rs:1509, 1542, 1551). In production, out-of-range parameter values and malformed valid_range metadata load completely silently, meaning the diagnostic feature is effectively dead code from the user's perspective."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-70c8111f","decision":"reject","rationale":"The legacy _mg/_mg_total fields store total-mass kinetic half-saturation constants that are scientifically meaningful only when expressed as concentrations. The normalization in provenance_value() correctly converts them to mg/L (or mg/m² for plant area parameters). Making this opt-in risks showing raw total-mass values as if they were concentrations, which is scientifically misleading. The real defects — ambiguous fallback formatting with empty ParamMeta (lines 648-658) and the undocumented valid_range contract — are better addressed by the documentation amendment (fr-3-25137feb) and surfacing diagnostics (fr-3-cb38a067), not by removing correct normalization."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-ce96654a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: ProcessParamsPreset has per-parameter param_meta: BTreeMap<String, ParamMeta> (line 505-508), but SourceWaterPreset (line 49) and ShrimpPreset (line 185) expose only file-level provenance: Option<Provenance>. Source-water chemistry and shrimp life-history parameters cannot carry per-parameter source, confidence, or range metadata, which is a real completeness gap if the acceptance criteria call for chemistry-and-biology coverage."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2870257c-b52b-4722-9d62-92f6fd49afdb"}
